ntial friction points for rapid iteration.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. My domain is technical viability AND speed/quality of prototyping. \n\nTechnical viability: High. This is standard MLOps infrastructure. 8/10 on feasibility.\nSpeed of prototyping impact: The \"mandatory documentation template integrated with our Git workflow to update records whenever parameters or training sets change\" — if this means every time I commit a model change, there's an additional step (even automated) in my pipeline, that's a small tax. But if it's truly automatic (CI generates the doc entry from metadata), then near-zero impact. The \"compliance officers review weekly\" doesn't block development.\n\nI'll approve at 72.\n",
