ess the core technical requirement of Art. 12 (ensuring logs are actually captured).\n- It builds a heavy system for what might be a lighter problem.\n- The \"constrained generation for legal precision\" is a red flag for resource commitment without clear deliverable.\n\nI'll reject it with a moderate-low promise score, maybe around 30-40. The underlying goal has merit but the implementation is misaligned with my efficiency concerns and doesn't address the primary regulatory obligation.\n\nLet me settle on: reject, promise 35.\n",
