cientific impact? It touches the frontier, has moderate intellectual merit (the predictive failure question is real but under-specified), and offers potential but not guaranteed broader impact. I think it clears a modest bar for approval as a research direction worth exploring with resources, though it would need sharpening. Actually, let me reconsider — \"approving means committing scarce implementation resources.\" Is this specific enough to commit to? The proposal describes a multi-year cross-disciplinary program without clear milestones or falsifiable hypotheses. From a pure intellectual merit standpoint, the core question (which operational events are predictive of AI system failure) is worth investigating, but the proposal as written is more of a vision than a research plan with clear scientific contributions identifiable.\n\nI'll approve it but at a moderate score — it's a legitimate frontier question with real impact potential, even if under-specified. Score: 60.\n",
