atory compliance, this is a valuable infrastructure piece that directly supports our obligation to maintain accurate, current technical documentation. It reduces the risk of non-compliance due to human error or neglect in documentation maintenance.\n\nI would approve this because:\n1. It directly addresses Recital 71's \"kept up to date\" requirement for technical documentation.\n2. It reduces compliance risk (documentation drift is a well-known failure mode).\n3. It supports our ability to demonstrate compliance during audits.\n4. It preserves prototyping speed, which means the lab can continue developing while staying compliant - institutional survival.\n5. The scope is appropriate as one component of a broader Article 12 compliance strategy (not claiming to be the whole solution).\n\nThe promise score: This is genuinely useful from my vantage point. It's not a complete Article 12 solution (doesn't handle runtime logging), but it addresses a critical and persistent compliance risk. I'd rate this around 78-82. It's clearly valuable, well-scoped, and directly supports regulatory obligations. But it's one piece of the puzzle, so not a 90+.\n\nLet me settle on: approve, promise 80.\n",
