lectual merit of research (it may actually constrain exploratory freedom), and has negligible direct impact on broader scientific reach. Its value is real but belongs to other functions (legal, engineering, operations).\n\n**Promise score:** From my specific vantage point (knowledge frontier, intellectual merit, broader scientific impact), this proposal scores quite low. It's not harmful — it's just irrelevant to my concerns. I'd put it around 10-15. It has a tiny sliver of indirect value (richer data from logging could theoretically feed research), but the proposal as stated is purely process-oriented. I'll go with 12.\n",
