nding meetings, providing input) but not LEADING with our scarce resources. The proposal as written asks us to lead, which crosses my threshold for resource commitment given compliance priorities.\n\nI'll reject it. Promise score: maybe 35-40. There's genuine value in the idea of common schemas, and the reputation angle is real. But \"lead a multi-institutional working group\" with scarce resources, for an instrument that has no legal force under the Act, when our primary obligation is to build compliant logging into our actual systems — this doesn't clear my bar as something to commit implementation resources to right now.\n\nLet me settle on 38.\n",
