        "content": "{\n  \"screenings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"P1988\",\n      \"rationale\": \"While automated documentation from MLflow trackers and version control metadata is a sensible building block for the technical-documentation obligations in Recital 71, this proposal is scoped to the prototyping/development phase and addresses development artefacts (hyperparameters, dataset hashes, validation metrics) rather than Article 12's core requirement: automatic recording of operational events over the system's full lifetime. It does not cover the specific log fields mandated by Art. 12(3) for Annex III 1(a) systems (use-period timestamps, reference-database identifiers, matched input data, verifier identity), nor does it address post-market monitoring logs under Art. 72 or substantial-modification triggers under Art. 12(2)(a). From a regulatory-survival standpoint, deploying this as our Article 12 answer would leave critical audit gaps that a market-surveillance authority or notified body could flag immediately.\",\n      \"decision\": \"reject\",\n      \"promise\": 35\n    }\n  ]\n}",
        "reasoning_content": "The user wants me to evaluate proposal P1988 as a Compliance Officer of an R&D institution developing AI systems subject to the EU AI Act. My domain of concern is institutional survival, regulatory compliance, and market reputation.\n\nLet me analyze this proposal from my compliance perspective:\n\n**Proposal P1988: Automated Technical Documentation Pipeline**\n\nThe proposal describes a tool that auto-generates compliance reports using training logs and version control metadata. It converts raw experiment data into structured regulatory documentation by pulling hyperparameters, dataset hashes, and validation metrics from MLflow trackers to populate EU AI Act templates automatically, integrated into CI/CD pipeline. The stated goal is removing manual burden from engineers while maintaining development velocity during prototyping.\n\n**Compliance Assessment:**\n\nStrengths:\n- Directly supports Article 12(1) - automatic recording of events/logs over lifetime. MLflow trackers + version control metadata provide a structured, timestamped record trail.\n- Supports Recital 71's requirement for \"clear and comprehensive form\" documentation containing algorithms, data, training, testing, validation processes.\n- Dataset hashes provide traceability (Recital 71: \"traceability of those systems\").\n- Integration into CI/CD means the logging is continuous and automatic - aligns with Article 12(1)'s \"technically allow for the automatic recording.\"\n- Hyperparameters and validation metrics address Recital 71's requirement for documentation on \"training, testing and validation processes used.\"\n- Version control metadata supports lifetime tracking.\n\nConcerns/Weaknesses:\n- The proposal focuses heavily on prototyping phase (\"maintaining high development velocity during prototyping\"). Article 12 requires logging over the LIFETIME of the system, not just development. Post-market monitoring (Art. 72), substantial modification detection (Art. 12(2