ia vague.\n\nMy decision: This is borderline. The underlying engineering (log analytics pipeline) is viable and useful, but the proposal as written is too research-oriented and open-ended for my speed/quality-of-prototyping mandate. It doesn't specify concrete prototype deliverables, integration points, or performance targets. As a development engineer who needs to commit scarce implementation resources, I can't back something that has no defined engineering milestone and whose success criteria are \"publish a methodology.\"\n\nI'll reject it but give it a moderate promise score because the underlying technical direction (log analytics for AI systems) is sound and could be reframed as a concrete engineering project.\n",
