se score should be high - maybe 82-85. Not 100 because there are integration complexities and the \"eliminates manual overhead\" claim is aspirational rather than realistic, but the core technical approach is sound and well-bounded.\n\nLet me settle on a score: I'd say 83. It's very promising from a dev/prototyping standpoint - clear scope, existing tools, fast iteration possible - but the full \"elimination of manual overhead\" is an overpromise that will create expectations gaps during implementation.\n",
