        "content": "{\n  \"screenings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"P2370\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The intersection of interpretability and regulatory logging is a scientifically interesting space, and capturing reasoning traces beyond timestamps could advance knowledge about how transformer-based systems arrive at decisions. However, the proposal as stated lacks any specific scientific hypothesis, identifies no concrete gap in existing XAI/mechanistic-interpretability literature that its 'new latent space recording techniques' would fill, and offers no methodology or success metrics—making it read as a strategic slogan ('transforms a legal requirement into a breakthrough') rather than a rigorous research program. From the knowledge-frontier vantage point, I cannot confirm this will generate novel understanding distinct from what major interpretability groups are already pursuing.\",\n      \"decision\": \"reject\",\n      \"promise\": 42\n    }\n  ]\n}",
